From 0817d2e9624f1d7b6bde53e6c1b00f5cccd78ce0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:50:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] provider: a sub2api plan sold by shares reads as a share, not
 dollars (#3188, wtj-0527)

A sub2api deployment can sell a plan shared out by shares: a key has no
dollar cap, only a share of each 5h/7d window, and its /v1/usage says so
with "unit": "percent" on each rate_limits entry. magpie read every window
as dollars, so the card said "37.5 / 100 USD" for a key that spent no
money, and Check balance / magpie provider show said "$20.00".

readSub2APIKeyLimits now reads such a window as the share used alone, with
no Amount, Limit or Unit, so QuotaWindow.Count (and the GUI's quotaCount)
says nothing of it, the way a subscription's window reads. Balance, whose
dollar sum moved to windowsLeft, gives the share the fullest window has
left, "20%". A window with no unit, "USD" or anything else reads as before,
and KeyAllowance is unchanged since it goes by Used.

Red, on unmodified 6afbe3f3:
  go test -tags nogui ./internal/provider/ -count=1 -run 'TestSub2APIKeySharesAreNotDollars'
  sub2api_usage_test.go:124: 5 hours = {Unlimited:false Name:5 hours Used:37.5
  ResetsAt:... Amount:37.5 Limit:100 Unit:USD ...} Span:5h0m0s ...}

Green, with the change:
  go test -tags nogui ./internal/provider/ -count=1 -run 'TestSub2APIKeySharesAreNotDollars'
  ok  github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/provider  0.014s

Also green: TestReadSub2APIKeyLimits, TestSub2APIKeyLimitsOnItsCard and
every TestKeyAllowance* unchanged; the whole package passes with
-skip TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials, which fatals ("close of
synctest channel from outside bubble") identically on unmodified 6afbe3f3
on this machine. gofmt -l is clean; go vet -tags nogui ./internal/provider/
and go build -tags nogui ./... pass. The fixture is the issue's example
reply byte for byte.
